A||||6||Bautsch||Service Eng. Soon????????
Z||000000||Bautsch||09-02-99||06:38 PM||||What is the service eng. soon dummy light connected to on the 88 4cylinder ? The Light keeps coming on and off on mine and I'm not sure what to service.<p>Thanks,<br>Mike Bautsch<br>mike@macvend.com
Z||000001||Gokart||09-02-99||06:56 PM||||Get yourself a GM scanner and place it in the ECM, behind cigarette lighter panel, and according to instructions in the book they enclose. The engine light will flash code(s) and can be deciphered with book as well. Good luck. 
Z||000002||batboy||09-02-99||07:34 PM||||Often, the service engine light means that a electronic fuel injection sensor is going bad. I'd get it checked out.
Z||000003||Ozzy||09-02-99||08:45 PM||||I did not use a scanner to find out what codes were in the ECM. The Haynes manual has the codes in it. These are deciphered according to how many times the 'Service Engine Soon' light flashes when you put the ECM into diagnostic mode. <p>You do that by shorting 2 terminals in the ALCL connector that Gokart described behind the cigar lighter panel.(2 small Torx screws) If you were to look at the connector from the front of the vehichle, it would be the bottom left 2 terminals. (A & B according to the Haynes book) When you short these, the Service Engine light should give a flashing sequence of '1 flash, pause, 2 flashes.'It will do this sequence three times, then any following sequences will be stored codes unless there are none in which case the same initial sequence will repeat itself.<p>I did not know this either and worked it out fairly quickly to determine codes. These are also defined in the Haynes book which give you a place to begin lookin for your problem.<br>There is also a web site that has them broken down; I will post it if I can find it again. I HATE the Haynes manual and would not recommend it to anyone if there is another option.<p>Ozzy
Z||000004||Ozzy||09-02-99||09:28 PM||||Just found that site:<p>http://www.euronet.nl/users/fo_elmo/techno.htm<p>Has some other interesting stuff too.<p>Ozzy<p>
Z||000005||K9||09-03-99||05:42 AM||||Go with what ozzy says. I have followed the steps in the Haynes book and it is very stright-forword. <br>Good luck!
Z||000006||Andy||09-03-99||05:59 PM||||I agree with Ozzy and K9,but make sure to disconnect you're battery for a minute after you found you're problem and fixed it[to clear the ECM memory]otherwise you're Service light will probably keep coming on
